# bug — Real Bug-Version Generator

When the user asks to **create a bug version**, **inject bugs**, **make a bug drill**, or **set up a QA kata**, use this tool.

## Quick commands

```bash
# Safe mode — creates sibling directories, never touches the original
python ~/.bug/scripts/make_bug_version.py <source> --profile messy --count 12

# In-place — only for sandbox/examples/training directories
python ~/.bug/scripts/inject_bug.py <sandbox> --count 3

# Shorthand if bug is on PATH
bug bug-version <source> --profile messy --count 12
bug inject <sandbox> --bug comparison-flip
```

## Supported source languages

Python · JS/TS · Go · Rust · Java · Kotlin · Swift · C# · C/C++ · Ruby · PHP

## Profiles

- `soft` — subtle logic regressions, safe for beginners
- `messy` — real-world mix (default)
- `chaos` — everything including crash-inducers

## Key bug types

| Type | Language | Effect |
|------|----------|--------|
| `nil-check-flip` | Go | Flips `err != nil` — swallows errors |
| `unwrap-panic` | Rust | `unwrap_or(x)` → `unwrap()` — panics on None |
| `equals-to-ref` | Java | `.equals()` → `==` — reference vs value |
| `force-unwrap` | Swift | `?? x` → `!` — crashes on nil |
| `comparison-flip` | all | `===` → `!==`, `<=` → `<` etc. |
| `off-by-one` | all | loop bounds shift by 1 |
| `missing-await` | JS/TS/C#/Rust | removes one `await` |
| `sort-direction` | all | reverses sort order |
| `shared-reference` | all | removes defensive copy |

## Workflow

1. Run `make_bug_version.py` against the clean source.
2. Read `BUG_VERSION_MANIFEST.json` — it records every mutation (file, line, before/after).
3. Present the bug-version to the solver; keep the manifest as the answer key.
4. To reset: run the same command again (it rebuilds from the clean source).

## Safety

- **Never** modify the original source directory.
- **Never** inject into production, auth, billing, or deployment code.
- Always write a manifest so every change is auditable and reversible.
